Explanation of the fix:

1. We add `handleOnInputFocus`, which locates the nearest parent ListBox container (using the `.${prefix}--list-box` CSS class) and calls its `focus()` method.
2. We hook that into the `<input>` by extending the `getInputProps` call with `onFocus: this.handleOnInputFocus`.  

With this in place, clicking into the input will immediately transfer focus to the wrapping `<ListBox>` node, causing its focus outline (the blue border around the whole control) to appear instead of the narrower outline on the text input.
